#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 780.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079423} :activity/id #uuid "ff014b49-75da-5266-b4b5-9e7bd3e5b3d8" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048186 :topic/id #uuid "869fb66c-d668-58cf-9dd4-b10651dbe9d5" :topic/math-academy-id 634} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079423 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079675 :tutorial/content "Suppose we are given the graph of ![](images/c9/c956e6cbfb2d94fa56a68a3173ec78f60fee33a9066c9c44ca4096d67d7b1cba.svg) shown below.\n\n![](images/2c/2cb61ee785ff6e04c5b73281389d6653f42bc93636da6840fbc2391ffb82451c.png)\n\nHow can we use graph transformations to plot the graph of\n\n![](images/c5/c546f9b96ef07d40050b7d98f046528f54ea43afc5d42c1bac48d2a02406e079.svg)\n\nSince this function involves several transformations, we apply them in the following order:\n\n1\\. First, we perform the transformations *inside* the argument of ![](images/a0/a047a10a3ed3f5e86676e8fca21093abfe6a1849d90ce94b62101f34fca37e3d.svg) We first carry out horizontal stretches, followed by horizontal translations.\n\n2\\. Then, we perform the transformations *outside* the argument of ![](images/a0/a047a10a3ed3f5e86676e8fca21093abfe6a1849d90ce94b62101f34fca37e3d.svg) We first carry out vertical stretches, followed by vertical translations.\n\nIn this case, we begin by factoring out the coefficient next to the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg) inside the function: \n\n![](images/e9/e905676d5234ac091212cf51bce10510cdde7e6c5000aabb564dfee38ca4c020.svg)\n\nNow, to plot ![](images/18/1867234b91fecd21c650bf6b29134a695d20150a98990c6c7b65ffed0a858a8a.svg) we apply the following steps:\n\n- Consider the curve ![](images/e2/e2ed4a9881134f510823ba710f835acf5720b866f0df86fa6cd24448524431d6.svg)\n\n- Stretch it by a scale factor of ![](images/9a/9ae11798da63cafee6ce5ccf824a7b96f9f7407a4ee445d1431d907c36f5dd1b.svg) parallel to the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-axis to get the graph of ![](images/a1/a142ed820c2bdafb8c1b7969028c7f4533c66fa772a73954c46f6b5eb91a050f.svg)\n\n![](images/07/07fe84bddbdc721dfba2fc9b720ca79ff794e9846fa1ef3bbc0c3c2217edd4e8.png)\n\n- Then, translate it to the right by ![](images/f5/f5f3224583db57b9cfe323c8489ef5e5271000002b5ea253eb98fd067a858b2d.svg) units to get the graph of ![](images/d0/d027e035caec097035ee8f20e49d28dadb156445265efe674460854cce152406.svg)\n\n![](images/a1/a16ccd8e56c64f80f93476f2b7a41aa3093a2e4b9fdbe089fa502d1f1df15923.png)\n\n- There is no vertical scaling, so we omit this step.\n\n- Finally, translate it up by ![](images/95/95836ae470c61ab15bfb67d6f0c92d2ad8d03d400b04473e81e58de3ee44bf32.svg) unit to get the graph of ![](images/f6/f6d6c8ff90e58f882bbd48d3b52f37f8c1657a5a45218d31c481c2a400e25ac3.svg)\n\n![](images/f4/f4a894860fadbc3ac88fa360cae23ef0f33903f3d930cb00496bb2c2505d2334.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "bf539881-a530-50df-b39d-b9718839371f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4616 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "e6e20122-6866-5fbc-9527-7a17b8c290e8" :step/math-academy-id 28409 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079425}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079424 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078510 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078360 :question/id #uuid "bbd2751e-73b2-500b-abef-c67564a9559f" :question/math-academy-id "e-7622"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c2387a4-202d-528a-b0ca-3f87d5a06ea3" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079219} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079220} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526016} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526069}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Correct Order of Transformations Given a Transformed Function Expression"} :step/id #uuid "a78dc881-a3e2-5e40-bd1b-cf28fe897545" :step/math-academy-id 28411} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186079425 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078511 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078361 :question/id #uu